@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>.
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>.
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>.
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>.
@prefix : <http://example.org/odp#>.

:Ontology a owl:Ontology ;
  rdfs:label "Author Pseudonyms Ontology" ;
  rdfs:comment "An ontology for managing an author's pseudonyms and their works.".

:Author a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Author" ;
  rdfs:comment "A person who writes books under different names.".

:Pseudonym a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Pseudonym" ;
  rdfs:comment "An alternative name used by an author to publish books.".

:hasPseudonym rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:domain :Author ;
  rdfs:range :Pseudonym ;
  rdfs:label "hasPseudonym" ;
  rdfs:comment "Relates an author to a pseudonym.".

:Book a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Book" ;
  rdfs:comment "A written work published by an author.".

:writtenBy rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:domain :Book ;
  rdfs:range :Author ;
  rdfs:label "writtenBy" ;
  rdfs:comment "Relates a book to the author who wrote it.".

:publishedAs rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:domain :Book ;
  rdfs:range :Pseudonym ;
  rdfs:label "publishedAs" ;
  rdfs:comment "Relates a book to the pseudonym under which it was published.".

Scenario-requirement-to-axiom mapping:
1. Under what pseudonym did the author C. S. Lewis published a collection of poems, Spirit in Bondage?
   - :Book, :writtenBy, :hasPseudonym, :publishedAs

2. What alternative did C. S. Lewis use to assume the role of a book writer?
   - :Author, :hasPseudonym

3. Show the trajectories of rivers which cross national parks?
   - This requirement is not grounded in the scenario or CQs, so it is not included in the ontology.

Intentionally excluded concepts:
- Rivers and national parks: These concepts are not present in the scenario or CQs, so they are not included in the ontology.